    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hi \u2014 I'd like to help with this if it's not already spoken for.\n\nI've been looking at PR #818's method design (trait/macro/type-state layer), and this issue looks like a clean, self-contained split from that: the `LolaMethodCaller`/`LolaMethodHandler` in `com-api-runtime-lola/method.rs` are currently `todo!()` placeholders, and per this issue's description the intent is to implement them following the existing Event backend's FFI pattern in the same crate.\n\nBefore I start: is anyone (e.g. @bharatGoswami8) already actively working on this piece as part of #818? Don't want to duplicate effort. If it's open, my plan is to first map the Event backend's existing FFI calls against the Method trait surface from #818's design doc, sketch how that maps onto Methods, and post that here before writing any code.",
