    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@bharatGoswami8 @LittleHuba \n\nI\u2019ll leave the rest as comments on the issue. But I want to clarify two things right now:\n\nFirst \u2014 on the sync/async bridge strategy: For milestone 1, can we just wrap the synchronous LoLa call in an already-resolved future? Or do you want real async dispatch from the start? Because issue 767 might actually go away if we do real async instead of blocking a thread.\n\nAnd second \u2014 on scope: Is E2E protection for Rust Methods and Fields part of 782\u2019s first milestone, or should that be a separate issue? I searched the repo and there\u2019s no E2E issue at all right now.",
